  the proposal, with no required lifetime or retirement work deferred.

Phase 18 — Review remaining bandwidth and validate the combined result
  ☐ Obtain a matched optimized-build comparison after executable-lifetime fixes.
    - Separate preparation, water-depth, volume-boundary, surface/OIT, pre-overlay capture and
      ordinary composition costs using existing profiling owners where possible.
    - Compare affected quality/resolution selections and at least a water-heavy and dry view;
      retain build/settings details alongside results. No fixed FPS target is assumed.
  ☐ Investigate remaining volume-target and composition bandwidth only if measurements justify it.
    - Two full-resolution RGBA32F volume targets remain a known cost; storage size is not bandwidth.
    - Evaluate coverage restriction or compatible pass/resource reuse before changing precision.
    - Do not blindly switch signed accumulation to RGBA16F, remove required backfaces, or enable
      depth rejection that loses valid entry/exit boundaries. Any such change needs a separate
      documented numerical/visibility justification and focused regression coverage.
    - Keep measured findings with no justified implementation explicitly documented as such.
  ☐ Review focused regressions, linked documentation and user-run visual/performance feedback.
